# Environments

| | local | preview (per PR) | production |
| :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- |
| host | your machine | Dokploy on the-keep | Vercel (api, web, dashboard) |
| database | `pnpm db:up` Postgres :5435 | Postgres per PR on the homelab | Neon |
| files | optional Garage | Garage bucket `ceraghit-dev`, prefix `pr-<n>/` | Cloudflare R2 + public CDN url |
| payments | demo gateway | demo gateway | no card gateway |
| data | `pnpm db:seed` | seeded on start (catalogue + demo orders) | real catalogue via `pnpm db:seed:catalog`, never demo |
| `APP_ENV` | local | preview | production |

- `apps/api/src/env.ts` enforces this: production requires R2 + `DEPLOY_ENV=production` and forbids demo seed and
  `ONLINE_PAYMENTS=true`. `apps/api/test/env.test.ts` covers it.
- Aramex: previews use the test host (or `ARAMEX_FAKE`), live only in production (`docs/aramex.md`).
- Outside production every email goes to `MAIL_REDIRECT_TO`, production refuses it.
- Secrets are scoped by GitHub Environment (`preview`, `production`). Production secrets (`DATABASE_URL`, R2,
  Vercel token) must not be readable from preview workflows.
- Production migrations run in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` before the deploy. `BOOTSTRAP` (migrate + seed on boot) is
  on for local/preview and off in production.

Staging is a fifth case: `main` redeployed on every merge on the-keep at fixed hosts (`staging.yml`), preview-grade
(`APP_ENV=preview`, `DEPLOY_ENV=staging`, demo payments, bucket prefix `staging/`). It is not production and never
holds live keys.

# Payments

- No card gateway is integrated. Production offers cash on delivery, transfer and Payoneer only (`gatewayReady`); local,
  preview and e2e use the demo gateway for "online".
- Flow: `orders.create` holds stock (45 min), calls `payments.init`, returns `payUrl`; the customer comes back to
  `/order/<number>?t=<token>` and `orders.get` calls `settleOrder`.
- `settleOrder` asks the gateway and only marks paid when status is completed **and** amount, currency and order number
  match. It never judges an order opened with another gateway.
- The only other way to paid is `markPaidManually` (admin only, audited in `order_audit`), for transfers and Payoneer links
  the gateway never sees. It refuses card orders and an amount or currency the owner did not see. Each call stores who,
  when, method and note; only the owner can call it, never customer or gateway data.
- Keep new gateways behind `PaymentProvider` (`docs/payments.md`).
- Pieces are `quoteOnly` (no cart, "ask for a quote") when they are commissions or too expensive for card checkout.

# Provider secrets

- Provider keys saved in the dashboard live AES-256-GCM encrypted in `integration_credentials`, master key
  `SECRETS_KEY` (differs per environment, api only, optional until a provider reads the vault). They are never returned to a client or logged: read them server side
  with `getSecret(services, provider)`, show only `admin.integrations.*` masks. Details in `docs/secrets.md`.

# Scheduled jobs

- Job shape is in `AGENTS.md`. The scheduler holds only the api URL and `CRON_SECRET` and calls production; previews have
  no schedules.
